.TH ZLOAD 1 "September 2026" "zload 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zload \- ultra-fast, zero-friction Zsh plugin manager and loader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zload
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISPEC\fR...]
.br
.B zload
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBzload\fR is an ultra-fast, zero-friction plugin manager and loader for Zsh.
It is engineered to deliver sub-millisecond warm startup latency (< 0.5 ms)
by consolidating declared plugins into a single static file, compiling it directly
into memory-mapped Zsh wordcode (\fI.zwc\fR), automatically resolving canonical
execution order, and completely eliminating subprocess forks during interactive shell launch.

.SH DECLARATION SYNTAX
\fBzload\fR supports multiple flexible input formats:
.TP
.B Native Zsh Array (Recommended)
Store plugins in a standard Zsh array and pass by expansion:
.RS
.nf
plugins=(
  casonadams/zline
  romkatv/powerlevel10k
  omz:git
  lukechilds/zsh-nvm --on nvm,node,npm
  zsh-users/zsh-syntax-highlighting --defer
  zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions
)
zload "${plugins[@]}"
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Multiline Quoted String
Pass a block of specifications separated by linebreaks:
.RS
.nf
zload "
  romkatv/powerlevel10k
  omz:git
  zsh-users/zsh-syntax-highlighting --defer
  zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions
"
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Line-by-Line Invocations
Call \fBzload\fR individually across your \fI~/.zshrc\fR:
.RS
.nf
zload romkatv/powerlevel10k
zload omz:git
.fi
.RE

.SH SUPPORTED SOURCES
.TP
\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Standard GitHub repository, cloned shallowly via \fBgit clone --depth 1\fR.
.TP
\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR@\fItag\fR
Pins the repository to a specific release tag.
.TP
\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR#\fIbranch\fR
Tracks a specific Git branch.
.TP
\fBomz:\fR\fIplugin\fR
Fetches an Oh-My-Zsh plugin from a shared shallow repository checkout. Automatically sources required library dependencies (such as \fIlib/git.zsh\fR) and adds completion directories to \fB$fpath\fR.
.TP
\fBomz:themes/\fR\fItheme\fR
Loads an Oh-My-Zsh theme file and injects prompt color and git helpers.
.TP
\fBomz:lib/\fR\fIfile.zsh\fR
Loads an Oh-My-Zsh core library directly.
.TP
\fBprezto:\fR\fImodule\fR
Loads a Prezto module and autoloads all functions in its \fIfunctions/\fR directory.
.TP
\fBsnippet:\fR\fIurl\fR
Downloads a single script file via \fBcurl\fR without cloning a Git repository, saves it in a managed directory, and byte-compiles it to \fI.zwc\fR.
.TP
\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR \fB--from gh-r\fR
Queries the GitHub Releases API, identifies the precompiled binary asset matching the host operating system and CPU architecture, extracts the archive, and exports the binary directly into \fB$PATH\fR.
.TP
\fIurl\fR
Clones an arbitrary remote Git repository (e.g. GitLab, Bitbucket, self-hosted).
.TP
\fIpath\fR
Loads a local plugin directory from disk (resolves \fB~\fR and relative paths).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--on\fR \fIcommand1,command2\fR
Registers lightweight proxy stub functions for the specified commands. Startup latency is 0 ms; the plugin is sourced only when one of the commands is executed for the first time.
.TP
\fB--on-dir\fR \fIpattern\fR
Defers loading until the working directory matches \fIpattern\fR or contains a signature file matching \fIpattern\fR (e.g. \fI.git\fR or \fIpackage.json\fR). Hook deregisters upon match.
.TP
\fB--defer\fR, \fB--idle\fR
Schedules plugin loading immediately after the initial prompt is rendered via \fBprecmd\fR. Sources immediately in non-interactive sessions.
.TP
\fB--path\fR, \fB--subpath\fR \fIdir\fR
Targets a specific subdirectory inside a mono-repository for script and completion discovery.
.TP
\fB--build\fR, \fB--hook\fR \fIcommand\fR
Executes \fIcommand\fR inside the cloned directory right after installation and upon Git updates. Zero runtime overhead during normal shell startup.
.TP
\fB--bin\fR \fIdir\fR
Adds a custom subdirectory to \fB$PATH\fR.
.TP
\fB--from\fR \fIgh-r|github-releases\fR
Installs precompiled release binaries from GitHub Releases assets.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBzload path\fR [\fIdirectories...\fR]
Safely prepends directories to \fB$PATH\fR. Automatically validates that each directory exists on disk, expands \fB~\fR and variables, and applies strict global deduplication. Running with no arguments prints the active \fB$PATH\fR one entry per line.
.TP
\fBzload fpath\fR [\fIdirectories...\fR]
Prepends directories to \fB$fpath\fR with validation and deduplication.
.TP
\fBzload eval\fR \fIname\fR \fIcommand\fR
Caches the shell output of a subshell initializer (such as \fBstarship init zsh\fR or \fBzoxide init zsh\fR) into a compiled \fI.zwc\fR wordcode file. On subsequent launches, sources the cache in 0.2 ms with zero child process forks.
.TP
\fBzload update\fR [\fB--self\fR|\fB--all\fR|\fB-f\fR|\fB--force\fR]
Updates installed Git plugins and remote snippets in parallel, reporting commit diffs and re-running build hooks when changes are pulled. Pass \fB-f\fR to discard local working tree modifications and force updates. Pass \fB--self\fR to update only \fBzload\fR itself, or \fB--all\fR to update both \fBzload\fR and all plugins. Recompiles the wordcode bundle upon completion.
.TP
\fBzload upgrade\fR [\fB-f\fR|\fB--force\fR], \fBzload self-update\fR [\fB-f\fR|\fB--force\fR]
Upgrades \fBzload\fR itself to the latest commit from upstream Git, recompiles internal modules into wordcode, clears the runtime cache, and reloads updated functions in the active shell. Pass \fB-f\fR to discard local working tree changes before pulling.
.TP
\fBzload clean\fR [\fB-f\fR|\fB--force\fR]
Identifies unreferenced plugin directories on disk. Pass \fB-f\fR to delete unreferenced directories and flush stale bundle and completion caches from \fI~/.cache/zload\fR.
.TP
\fBzload list\fR
Displays all installed plugins with active Git branch, release tag, and commit SHA.
.TP
\fBzload which\fR \fIplugin\fR
Prints the full canonical filesystem directory of an installed plugin.
.TP
\fBzload cd\fR \fIplugin\fR
Changes the current working directory to the target plugin repository on disk.
.TP
\fBzload doctor\fR [\fB--fix\fR]
Runs comprehensive environment diagnostics. Pass \fB--fix\fR to automatically restore missing or stale \fI.zwc\fR wordcode files.
.TP
\fBzload profile\fR
Measures startup latency breakdown using microsecond timers.
.TP
\fBzload lock\fR [\fIfile\fR]
Exports all installed Git plugins and their resolved commit SHAs to a lockfile.
.TP
\fBzload sync\fR [\fIfile\fR]
Synchronizes all installed plugins to match the exact commit SHAs recorded in the lockfile.
.TP
\fBzload compile\fR
Recompiles the static bundle, core loader, and autoloaded functions into \fI.zwc\fR.
.TP
\fBzload compinit\fR [\fB--lazy\fR]
Initializes the completion system. Enabled automatically by default on plugin declarations unless \fBZLOAD_NO_COMPINIT\fR is set. When \fB--lazy\fR is specified (default), defers compinit until the first \fB<Tab>\fR keypress.
.TP
\fBzload help\fR
Displays summary usage information.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B ZLOAD_HOME
Root installation directory of \fBzload\fR (defaults to directory containing \fIzload.zsh\fR).
.TP
.B ZLOAD_DATA
Base directory for plugin repositories (defaults to \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/zload\fR or \fI~/.local/share/zload\fR).
.TP
.B ZLOAD_CACHE
Base directory for compiled bundles and dumps (defaults to \fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/zload\fR or \fI~/.cache/zload\fR).
.TP
.B ZLOAD_PLUGINS
Directory where cloned plugins are stored (defaults to \fI$ZLOAD_DATA/plugins\fR).
.TP
.B ZLOAD_NO_COMPINIT
If set to 1, disables automatic lazy completion system initialization.
.TP
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.zshrc
Primary Zsh configuration file where \fBzload\fR is invoked.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/zload/bundle.zsh.zwc
Compiled memory-mapped wordcode bundle containing all active plugins.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/zload/zcompdump-${ZSH_VERSION}.zwc
Compiled completion dump cache.
.TP
.I ~/.zfunc/
Standard custom completion directory. If present, automatically discovered and linked into \fB$fpath\fR by \fBzload\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
.B Clean Recommended ~/.zshrc:
.RS
.nf
# 1. Bootstrap zload (auto-clones on fresh machines)
if [ ! -d "${HOME}/.zload" ]; then
  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/casonadams/zload.git "${HOME}/.zload"
fi
source "${HOME}/.zload/zload.zsh"

# 2. PATH management
user_paths=(
  ~/.cargo/bin
  ~/.local/bin
  /opt/homebrew/bin
  /opt/homebrew/sbin
)
zload path "${user_paths[@]}"

# 3. Plugins
plugins=(
  omz:git
  omz:lib/completion.zsh
  casonadams/walh-shell
  lukechilds/zsh-nvm --on nvm,node,npm
  zsh-users/zsh-syntax-highlighting --defer
  zsh-users/zsh-autosuggestions
)
zload "${plugins[@]}"
bindkey '^ ' autosuggest-accept
.fi
.RE

